<h1>Launch StudyHub</h1>
<p class="lead">
  Follow these steps to run the JavaFX desktop application on your computer.
</p>

<h2>1. Check your prerequisites</h2>
<p>
  You need Git, JDK 17, and Maven installed, plus a desktop environment
  that can display application windows. Internet access is needed to
  download the repository and Maven dependencies.
</p>
<p>Open Terminal or your command prompt and run:</p>
<pre><code>git --version
java -version
mvn -version</code></pre>
<p>
  Confirm that Maven reports Java 17. If a command is not found,
  install the corresponding tool before continuing.
</p>

<h2>2. Obtain the project</h2>
<p>
  In a folder where you want a new copy of the project, run:
</p>
<pre><code>git clone https://github.com/ElAkaya/Studyhub.git
cd Studyhub</code></pre>
<p>
  If you already have the repository, open its existing folder instead
  of cloning it again. For example, on macOS:
</p>
<pre><code>cd ~/Downloads/Studyhub</code></pre>

<h2>3. Build and verify</h2>
<p>From the Studyhub repository folder, run:</p>
<pre><code>mvn -f code/studyhub-app/pom.xml clean verify</code></pre>
<p>
  Wait for Maven to finish downloading dependencies, compiling, and running
  its checks. Continue when the output reports BUILD SUCCESS.
</p>

<h2>4. Launch the application</h2>
<pre><code>mvn -f code/studyhub-app/pom.xml javafx:run</code></pre>
<p>
  The StudyHub desktop window opens. Leave the Terminal process running
  while you use the application.
</p>

<figure>
  <img src="/images/studyhub-home.png"
       alt="StudyHub main window with course selection, search, group list, and action buttons">
  <figcaption>
    The main window after creating an example group.
    Your group list may be empty when you first launch the application.
  </figcaption>
