<h2>5. Try your first group</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Click <strong>Create group</strong>.</li>
  <li>Enter a group name and select a catalog course.</li>
  <li>Fill in the description, meeting time, and location.</li>
  <li>Enter a positive whole number for <strong>Maximum members</strong>.</li>
  <li>Click <strong>Save group</strong>, then <strong>Show all</strong>
      to see the group in the main list.</li>
  <li>Select the group and click <strong>View details</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p>
  See the <a href="/features/create-group">create-group guide</a>
  for example values and validation help.
</p>

<h2>6. Close StudyHub</h2>
<p>
  Close the application window when finished. Groups exist only for
  the current session and are not retained when the application closes.
</p>

<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Maven uses the wrong Java version:</strong>
      configure JAVA_HOME for your JDK 17 installation, reopen Terminal,
      and check <code>mvn -version</code> again.</li>
  <li><strong>Maven cannot find the POM:</strong>
      run the commands from the Studyhub repository folder and confirm
      that <code>code/studyhub-app/pom.xml</code> exists.</li>
  <li><strong>Dependencies cannot download:</strong>
      check your internet connection and review the Maven error message.</li>
  <li><strong>No groups appear:</strong>
      create a group, then click <strong>Show all</strong> to clear filters.</li>
</ul>

